Building and installing CBoard
==============================

Requirements
------------

* A C compiler (GCC or Clang)
* CMake 3.16 or newer
* NCurses (wide-character build preferred: ncursesw)
* Curses menu and form libraries
* libviper / VDK (libvdk) — sibling checkout at ../libviper by default
* gettext / libintl (optional, for translations)
* libperl (optional, for the PERL plugin)

Build libviper first (once):

    cd ../libviper && cmake . && make

Basic build
-----------

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build
    sudo cmake --install build

If libviper is not a sibling of cboard:

    cmake -S . -B build -DLIBVIPER_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/libviper

Or with a custom prefix:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local
    cmake --build build
    cmake --install build

After installing, run "cboard -h" for command-line options, or start
"cboard" and press F1 for in-game help.

Common options
--------------

    -DWITH_LIBPERL=ON       Enable PERL plugin support (requires libperl)
    -DENABLE_DEBUG=ON       Enable debugging features
    -DENABLE_NLS=OFF        Disable gettext translations
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo

Example with PERL support:

    cmake -S . -B build -DWITH_LIBPERL=ON
    cmake --build build

PERL plugin
-----------

When built with -DWITH_LIBPERL=ON, pressing ^O filters the current game
through a PERL subroutine defined in ~/.cboard/perl.pl. The subroutine is
passed a generated FEN of the current position and should return a FEN after
processing.

Uninstall
---------

If you still have the build tree:

    cmake --build build --target uninstall

(If no uninstall target is present, remove the files listed in
build/install_manifest.txt.)
